      "environments.can_do": {
        "id": "environments.can_do",
        "kind": "atomic",
        "status": "implemented",
        "title": "What can be done in an environment (phone, server, directory, storage)",
        "description": "Answers from the graph: the environment is found among the environment nodes (a platform such as your phone or this server, a directory, a configured storage, an account at a service), its capabilities and accesses are read through their links, and the action engine says which actions of the catalogue fit them, with their effect flags and whether the rules allow, ask or deny. Accesses are shown as references to the secrets vault (a key name and whether it is set), never as secrets. Without an environment: the one this process runs in. Brings the derived environment nodes up to date first (setting environments_auto_sync).",
        "why": {
          "pl": "Odpowiada z grafu, co można zrobić w środowisku (telefon, serwer, katalog, magazyn)."
